  "narration": {
    "title": "The Yankees Own the Rotation, Boston Owns the Pen",
    "intro": "Pitching is the theme today, and two New York arms sit atop it. The Yankees have the best starting rotation in baseball, while Boston edges them for the deepest bullpen. Up front, Jacob Misiorowski and Cam Schlittler are throwing like the season belongs to them.",
    "staff_lead": "The Yankees lead the rotation board at a 3.28 starter ERA, with the Dodgers (3.48) and Detroit (3.51) close behind. It's quiet, steady company for the Tigers, a team still under .500 at 71-79 but pitching like a contender.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Boston tops the bullpen at a 3.11 reliever ERA, a nose ahead of the Yankees at 3.13. Atlanta, San Diego and Milwaukee round out the five, meaning the deepest pens and the best rotations mostly live in the same neighborhoods.",
    "arms_lead": "Misiorowski and Schlittler are tied at a 1.95 ERA, but the form scores split them: Misiorowski sits first at 95 with a 0.80 WHIP, Schlittler second at 91. Chris Sale holds third at 85, still the most dependable arm in Atlanta.",
    "risers_lead": "Not every arm is trending up. Foster Griffin dropped six to a 60 form, and Sandy Alcantara fell five to 56, the steepest slides among the arms that had been holding steady."
  }
